2026-11-19 03:15:23 - Agent_20261119031315 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed the two `py/regex-survey` results in `fastapi/utils.py`. Both are false positives for CWE-1333 (ReDoS) / CWE-407 (inefficient algorithm complexity):

1. `fastapi/utils.py:34` — `re.findall("{(.*?)}\", path)` in `get_path_param_names`. The pattern is a hardcoded compile-time string literal (no dynamic construction, so no regex injection). It contains no nested/ambiguous quantifiers capable of catastrophic backtracking: a single lazy `.*?` delimited by literal braces yields linear-time matching. Attacker-controlled `path` values only affect input length, not backtracking depth.

2. `fastapi/utils.py:124` — `re.sub("[^0-9a-zA-Z_]", "_", operation_id)` in `generate_operation_id_for_path`. A single negated character class with no quantifiers at all; strictly O(n) scan, structurally incapable of catastrophic backtracking.

Grep searches confirmed no other `re.`/regex usage in the flagged areas and no dynamic pattern construction feeding these sinks. Neither location is a genuine ReDoS or regex-injection vulnerability.
